  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-remote-agent",
      "text": "> English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n>\n> Deployment guide (Chinese): [dsh-remote-hub/docs/DEPLOY.zh.md](https://github.com/yhuan416/dsh-remote-hub/blob/main/docs/DEPLOY.zh.md)\n\nAgent-side DSH host plugin, installed on every backend a hub should reach."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-remote-agent",
      "text": "It publishes this process's launch token + identity to `$DSH_HOME/remote-agent.json`\n(0600, atomic write) and removes the file on shutdown. The token is generated per\nprocess and never persisted by dsh itself, so this file is the clean way for a hub to\nmint the browser cookie without scraping `journalctl`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"hostname\": \"yhuan-n100\",\n  \"pid\": 1234,"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "1) place the package where the profile can resolve it",
      "text": "mkdir -p ~/.dsh/plugins\ntar xzf dsh-remote-agent.tgz -C ~/.dsh/plugins\nln -sfn ~/.dsh/plugins/dsh-remote-agent ~/.dsh/profiles/node_modules/dsh-remote-agent\nln -sfn ~/.dsh/plugins/dsh-remote-agent ~/.dsh/profiles/web/node_modules/dsh-remote-agent"
    },
    {
      "section": "3) restart dsh web; then check",
      "text": "cat ~/.dsh/remote-agent.json\n```\n\nOptional config: `{ file: \"/custom/path/remote-agent.json\" }`.\n\nHub side pairs with `tokenFile: { kind: ssh, host, user, path: ~/.dsh/remote-agent.json }`."
    }
  ],
